[-] detoxification		<-->	n++[--0]	./diːˌtɒksɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/-NAmE /diːˌtɑːksɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/ [uncountable]
	;sự giải độc -- (1) ​(also informal detox) treatment given to people to help them stop drinking alcohol or taking drugs
		;a detoxification unit
		;Wordfinder: abuseaddictdealdependencedetoxificationdrughallucinateoverdoserehabwithdrawal
		;Topics Mental healthc2
	;sự thanh lọc -- (2) the process of improving the reputation of somebody/something that has been seen as morally bad
		;The policy has been key to the successful detoxification of the party's brand.
	;quá trình giải độc -- (3) the process of removing harmful substances or poisons from something
		;the detoxification of formaldehyde
	;;




